! FP sign-modifier load test (driven by the floating-point diagnostic
! jb_af1c, which uses LN/LA/LNA throughout): N inverts the operand's
! sign, A forces it positive, NA forces positive then inverts. The
! assembler could not encode these until this was added (verified
! bit-for-bit against jb_af1c in verify_fp_signmods.py).
!
! Each load reads a PRE-SET constant (never a word stored earlier in
! this program) so the test exercises only the sign modifiers, not the
! separate look-ahead store-close-to-fetch hazard documented in
! microarchitecture_plan.md (a store immediately before a load of the
! same word is a known gap).
!   LN(N),TWO    : +2.0 -> -2.0
!   LA(N),NEGTWO : -2.0 -> +2.0
!   LNA(N),TWO   : +2.0 -> force + then invert -> -2.0
START   LN(N), TWO
        ST(N), RNEG
        LA(N), NEGTWO
        ST(N), RABS
        LNA(N), TWO
        ST(N), RNA
DONE    BEW, $
        CNOP
TWO     DD(BU,64), 0
NEGTWO  DD(BU,64), 0
RNEG    DD(BU,64), 0
RABS    DD(BU,64), 0
RNA     DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
